ild]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:pt-0 md:[&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:mb-0"><h2 id="part-3-migrating-your-application-code-nextjs-example" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Part 3: Migrating your application code (Next.js example)</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#part-3-migrating-your-application-code-nextjs-example" aria-label="Link to Part 3: Migrating your application code (Next.js example)"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2><p>After migrating your database and user accounts, the final step is to update your application code to work with Neon Auth and the Neon Data API. This section guides you through refactoring a Next.js application from using Supabase&#x27;s client libraries (<code>@supabase/ssr</code>, <code>@supabase/supabase-js</code>) to using Neon Auth&#x27;s SDK (<code>@stackframe/stack</code>) and the standard <code>postgrest-js</code> library for data access.</p><p>The primary change in this migration is moving from Supabase&#x27;s single, integrated client library to a composable stack:</p><ol>
<li><strong>Authentication:</strong> You will replace Supabase Auth functions (<code>supabase.auth.getUser()</code>, custom middleware, and callback routes) with Neon Auth&#x27;s SDK. Neon Auth handles session management and provides simple hooks (<code>useUser</code>) and server-side helpers (<code>stackServerApp.getUser()</code>) to access user data.</li>
<li><strong>Data Access:</strong> You will replace the data access portion of the Supabase client (<code>supabase.from(...)</code>) with a dedicated PostgREST client (<code>postgrest-js</code>). The Neon Data API is PostgREST-compliant, meaning <strong>your query syntax (e.g., <code>.select()</code>, <code>.insert()</code>, <code>.eq()</code>) will remain almost identical.</strong> The main difference is how you initialize the client and authenticate requests using a JWT from Neon Auth.</li>
</ol><h3 id="step-1-update-project-dependencies" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight"><span>Step 1: Update project dependencies</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#step-1-update-project-dependencies" aria-label="Link to Step 1: Update project dependencies"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h3><p>First, remove the Supabase packages and install the PostgREST client library.</p><figure class="code-block group/code-block relative flex flex-col [&amp;_pre]:min-w-full rounded-none border border-gray-new-80 dark:border-gray-new-20 [&amp;&gt;pre]:my-0 [&amp;&gt;pre]:rounded-none [&amp;&gt;pre]:bg-white! [&amp;&gt;pre]:py-4 [&amp;&gt;pre]:dark:bg-black-pure!" data-has-filename="false" data-line-numbers="false"><pre class="shiki css-variables" style="background-color:var(--shiki-background);color:var(--shiki-foreground)" tabindex="0" data-language="bash"><code class="grid"><span class="line" data-line="1"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-comment)"># Remove Supabase libraries</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="2"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-function)">npm</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string)"> uninstall</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string)"> @supabase/ssr</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string)"> @supabase/supabase-js</span></span>
